{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789849540,"nonce":"HAiMhgWntOpM+U5P8CetR+5hQSc=","title":"scalar replacement read a predecessor OUT set that was not computed yet and seeded the field with undef","message":"`apply_sra` walked blocks once in BFS order and, for a predecessor not yet visited, used the undef baseline. An object allocated before a loop and read after it has the loop's condition block as a predecessor of the read, visited later in BFS order, so the field phi took `null` on that edge: `b.items` was null after any handle loop, and two `for (x in b)` loops in one function faulted in the second. The walk now iterates to a fixed point with stable phi and copy ids, so a loop-carried predecessor contributes the value it actually holds.","files":null}]}